  "240": {
    "caption": "We are thrilled to be bringing international bestselling author Ann Cleeves, the creator of Vera, Shetland, and The Long Call, to Charlottetown for the launch of her new novel The Dying Light. Ann will be in conversation with Mattea Roach, host of CBC\u2019s popular radio program Bookends. This is going to be a wonderful evening, don\u2019t miss out - get your tickets today!\n\nDate: Thursday, October 29th\nTime: 7 pm\nLocation: Delta Prince Edward\nCost: Book \u2013 Book and admission: $40 or Admission: $25\nFor tickets: https://bookmarkreads.ca/events/6329720261019\n\nNew York Times bestselling author Ann Cleeves returns with the fourth Two Rivers mystery featuring detective Matthew Venn. In The Dying Light, Venn and his team are called in to investigate a puzzling death. The body of a young woman has been found in the swimming pool of a lavish holiday home in North Devon, and her best friend is missing. Caught between a powerful family\u2019s secrets and a powder keg of local tensions, Venn must navigate a treacherous path. Knowing that the real answers lie not in what people say, but in the silence that they keep.\n\n#AnnCleeves #ReadingWritingAndWonder #DowntownCharlottetown\nPEI Public Library Service des biblioth\u00e8ques publiques \u00ceP\u00c9 Publishers Group Canada Pan Macmillan @followers\n\nOCR TEXT:\nMay be an image of text",
